# Sizing over scenarios (D-143), the reference case for plan/20-core-domain/24-auto-sizing.md.
#
# A changeover distribution loop: the same pipework carries hot water in winter and chilled water
# in summer. One plant, two duties, and the components must cover both.
#
# This sample exists for the trap in `24`. The duties say winter is the bigger case -- 50 kW against
# 40 -- but the *flows* say the opposite, because a chilled program is narrower:
#
#   winter  50 kW over 35/45 C  =  50 000 / (4180 * 10)  =  1.20 kg/s
#   summer  40 kW over  7/12 C  =  40 000 / (4180 *  5)  =  1.91 kg/s   <- 59 % more
#
# So every flow-driven size is governed by summer, the smaller duty, and a plant sized from the
# duty's winner alone is a pipe size short. The sizing report names the governing case per size.

fluidscript 1
scenarios winter summer
design winter

circuit distribution
fluid water

HE1  heat_exchanger power=[50, -40] in.t=[35, 12] out.t=[45, 7]   # source: boiler, then chiller
LOAD heat_exchanger power=[-50, 40] dp=0                          # the building, either way round
PU1  pump
P1   pipe length=20

connections
N1 - PU1 - N2 - HE1 - N3 - LOAD - N4 - P1 - N1
